{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01VGjpP5dUKBhPJc3NdpgA32","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the member document `anchor_gui.py`, here is the grounded session summary.\n\n## Summary â€” `anchor_gui.py` (Deliverables)\n\n**What it is**\n- `anchor_gui.py` is the Anchor application: a self-contained, stdlib-only Python HTTP server that serves an interactive web dashboard and exposes API endpoints so every UI action writes directly to the markdown source files, logs the change, and refreshes state (`anchor_gui.py:1-14`).\n\n**Key claims (grounded in the file)**\n- **Single-file, no external deps.** Imports are stdlib only â€” `json, logging, os, re, socket, sys, threading, time, traceback, webbrowser`, plus `http.server.ThreadingHTTPServer`/`BaseHTTPRequestHandler` and `urllib.parse` (`anchor_gui.py:16-21`).\n- **Path/data layer is centralized.** All file paths resolve through the shared `paths` helper, honoring `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR`; `DASHBOARD_MD`, `PROJECTS_MD`, `INBOX_MD`, `DOMAINS_DIR`, `LOGS_DIR`, `CANCELLED_MD`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER_MD` are derived from it (`anchor_gui.py:23-47`).\n- **Concurrency safety.** A process-wide `WRITE_LOCK` (from `paths`) is held around every markdown/JSON mutation so concurrent requests under `ThreadingHTTPServer` cannot lose an update; mutations go through a `_with_write_lock` wrapper (`anchor_gui.py:29-31`, `5316-5323`).\n- **Error/lifecycle logging.** Logs ERROR + INFO to `logs/errors.log`, with explicit guards against double FileHandler attach and propagation when the module is imported twice (e.g. by `anchor_healthcheck`) (`anchor_gui.py:49-71`).\n- **Cache-bust build identity.** A build id is computed once at startup from `git rev-parse --short HEAD`; the self-healing client JS uses it to force a cache-busting reload and clear stale service workers/Cache Storage on redeploy (`anchor_gui.py:74-90`, `144`).\n- **Task/markdown parsing + gathering.** Parsers read markdown into dicts â€” `parse_tasks_from_md`, `parse_projects_from_md`, `parse_inbox_from_md`, `parse_archived_tasks` â€” and `gather_all()` aggregates DASHBOARD + domain files (`anchor_gui.py:181-388`).\n- **Full task lifecycle ops.** `mark_done`/`mark_undone`, `add_task`, `capture_inbox`, `edit_task`, `edit_project`, `cancel_task`, `save_for_later`, `restore_task`, `link_task`, plus archive append helpers (`anchor_gui.py:5325-5751`).\n- **R&D cockpit render path.** Extensive R&D surface rendering â€” `render_project_window_html` (the large project-window builder), `_render_kanban_html`, lane tiles (`_render_lane_tile`/`_render_lane_sessions`), grass workbench (`_render_grass_workbench`), deliverable lane tiles, header rollup, and project tiles/rows (`anchor_gui.py:2139-2507`, `2507-5077`).\n- **v7 board integration is present.** Live registry sessions are bridged into the lane columns and deduped by session id â€” `_registry_session_view`, `_merge_registry_sessions`, `_gather_project_sessions` â€” and a session-summary-on-finish hook `_trigger_session_summary_on_finish` schedules a background summary on terminal transitions (`anchor_gui.py:1772-1914`, `991-1051`).\n- **Proactive summary triggers.** Background (daemon-thread) generators `_trigger_project_summary`, `_trigger_session_summary`, `_trigger_project_session_summaries`, and a continue-seed builder `_build_continue_seed` (`anchor_gui.py:906-1165`).\n- **Hand-rolled WebSocket + SSE terminal transport.** RFC-6455 codec helpers (`ws_accept_key`, `encode_text_frame`, `decode_frames`, â€¦) back the ConPTY terminal transports `_serve_term_ws`, `_serve_term_stream2`, `_serve_term_sse`, all token-gated via `_term_token_ok` (`anchor_gui.py:464-635`, `7798-8180`).\n- **Traversal-safe static asset routes.** `anchor_term_asset`, `xterm_asset`, `brand_asset` serve vendored assets with an `_unsafe_path_seg` guard (`anchor_gui.py:635-752`).\n- **HTTP handler.** `AnchorHandler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler)` implements `do_GET` (large route table, line 8180) and `do_POST` (line 8831) for the dashboard + `/api/*` + `/api/rnd/*` endpoints, with `_send_json`/`_send_html`/`_send_bytes` helpers (`anchor_gui.py:7765-9925`).\n- **Single-instance bind guard.** `_ExclusiveThreadingHTTPServer` overrides `server_bind` to bind exclusively (so a duplicate process exits cleanly rather than squatting port 8777); `make_server` defaults to `127.0.0.1:8777` and `resolve_bind_host` resolves the bind host (`anchor_gui.py:9936-9994`).\n- **Heartbeat watchdog.** A `_heartbeat_watchdog` thread monitors server liveness (`anchor_gui.py:9925`).\n\n**Scale / provenance note**\n- This is a large deliverable file (~10,088 lines). The claims above are grounded in the file's docstring, import block, and definition map; no run metrics or external test results are part of this session â€” the summary reflects the source as-is."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3475,"cache_read_input_tokens":65138,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3475},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cde3054f-f88d-417d-b1ee-4c5eaa78939a","uuid":"c2860ef5-c2b9-441d-bb43-ae90d7bb710e","request_id":"req_011Cc5QVfkajBCyiNKWfbASh"}
